Your bigger cost is JupyterLab

For your project, the cost hierarchy is roughly:

AWS resource	Cost concern
S3 CSV/model files	🟢 Very low
Serverless endpoint, no requests	🟢 No idle inference compute charge
Serverless endpoint, predictions	🟢 Pay per inference
JupyterLab ml.t3.medium running	🟠 Much more significant
SageMaker training job running	🟠 Costs while training

AWS specifically states that Serverless Inference scales to zero when there are no requests, so you don't pay for idle serverless resources.

For your setup, the main thing to remember is: STOP JupyterLab when you're finished working. Keep the Serverless endpoint only if you need to make predictions.

